{"id":"155a653a-36fa-47b9-b86b-42692852b6ee","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a3b618f11acb28d0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"36f12dcaf9fe46a3ea449eb9ba0e3c3d6dbc4c4e","start":7786,"end":7789},"shape":{"type":"Keyword","atoms":["try"]},"context":{"before":"1112eb3e712bbf2d","after":"2108d7ebf58f1db8"}},"payload":{"text":"AUTO-ATTACH: a terminal `node <file>` (node-runner's startDebug) — and a test file runs_tests runs, the same way —\npublishes `debug.launch`; start a tsval debug session for it, so running in the terminal IS a debug session\n(breakpoints, step-back, capability stops). Relay the session's end back on the `node.exit.<runId>` channel the\nterminal awaits; `debug.stop` (Ctrl-C) stops it. The runId rides in the launch config so start/terminate can correlate.\n\nGuarded end-to-end: this must NEVER break activate() (a failed bridge activation hangs the whole boot).\nIf any vscode.debug event API is missing here, we skip wiring AND fail `debug.launch` fast so the terminal\n(which awaits node.exit) doesn't hang.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:15:23.826Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:15:23.826Z"}
{"id":"1b61a331-66ba-4306-86eb-da5509fd7781","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"c6592c22590db579","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f383d5510e067223bef249ea4abd4614ba58814b","start":5327,"end":5367},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["registerDebugToolbar","(","context",",","bridgeHub",")"]},"context":{"before":"ef887ac866d67d6b","after":"c23d1d6f2c6f0b17"}},"payload":{"text":"The active session's toolbar, in the title bar of the preview window it drives too (debug-toolbar.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:15:29.842Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:15:29.842Z"}
