{"id":"e769602a-d4ac-469d-b3ca-fba874d55b11","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"208307d3a3f6b2fb","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f62d58f911c8c88e44614ec2e6aa33ca0a3c0aac","start":4738,"end":4766},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["registerDebugEvents","(","context",")"]},"context":{"before":"59322ec13fbb0b11","after":"a0506513b9c40d1b"}},"payload":{"text":"What every debugger's runs tell core — tsval's, and another extension's (`run.debugger`: an interpreter plugged in\nfrom editor-contrib) — the run contract's events, read the one way; and how each launch is resolved (debug-events.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:15:35.852Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:15:35.852Z"}
